.TH DANBY-KNUCKLEBALL 1
.SH NAME
danby-knuckleball \- fluctuating aerodynamic force on a knuckleball
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/knuckleball
.SH MODEL
In addition to quadratic drag, the vertical aerodynamic acceleration is
A sin(omega t).  The flutter amplitude and frequency expose the erratic force
created as the slowly rotating seams change orientation.  The pitch is followed
for 0.65 seconds or until ground impact.
.SH DISPLAY
The plots show height versus distance and speed versus time.  Tracks alter the
release, drag, flutter, frequency, and gravity.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/knuckleball.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR trajectory (2)
